base=DatabaseTask, bind=True)\ndef process_rows(self: task):\n    for row in self.db.table.all():\n        process_row(row)\n```\n\nThis change was made in a commit by Denys Pidlisnyi on July 28, 2022.\n\nThe example now correctly uses `self.db` instead of `process_rows.db`, which resolves the issue mentioned where `process_rows.db` would be None in other class methods such as `after_return`.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nNo further changes are needed as the documentation already reflects the correct usage with `bind=True`.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/9698/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/9698/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]